save(332,dict(paragraphs=["Manini Jena teaches Odia at Prananath College in Khordha. Alongside poetry, her journal biography records an interest in criticism of Odia stories and novels. That attention to literature’s making also enters her poems, where the act of writing becomes a subject to question rather than take for granted.","In ‘କବିତା ଲେଖୁଥିବା ଲୋକ’, poetry is discovered in fragrance, a labourer’s sweat and a cuckoo’s call, then threatened by noise and neglect. The poem asks whether writing words is enough to make a poet. ‘ସମୟ ପାଇଁ କିଛି ସମୟ’ turns instead towards withheld speech and the difficulty of apprehending time, giving abstract questions the pressure of breath, skin and the body."],sources=[source('Prananath College: Department of Odia','https://www.pnautonomouscollege.in/departments/odia',['Manini Jena listed as Odia Lecturer and Head; MA and MPhil; exact college and department match captured biography.'],'search_index_excerpt')],identity_match='Exact name plus Odia teaching at Prananath College agrees with captured biography; institutional faculty listing corroborates identity.',poems_read=[dict(id=752,title='କବିତା ଲେଖୁଥିବା ଲୋକ',basis='Full Odia original, two stanzas: fragrance, labour, cuckoo, mango scent, wounded poem, market noise and questions about authorship.'),dict(id=408,title='ସମୟ ପାଇଁ କିଛି ସମୟ',basis='Full Odia original: withheld speech, breath, questions as clothing, time and white shroud.')],limitations=['College page indexed successfully but direct opens with and without www failed. Current head designation omitted from prose to avoid overdating undated listing. Literary criticism interest attributed to captured journal biography. No verified book link found.'],next_action='Independent author/editor review; confirm any book bibliography.'))
